DATA MODEL
Model is based on fact table VISITS and dimension tables PROCEDURES, PROVIDERS, DATE TABLE, DEPARTMENTS, DIAGNOSES, INSURANCE, PATIENTS and CITIES (which is dimension table of PATIENTS).
 
The primary objectives of the dashboard were to provide a comprehensive overview of billing amounts and patient volumes over time, segmented by the procedures performed on patients. Additionally, the dashboard aimed to present the percentage contribution to the total billing amount from emergency patients, inpatients, and outpatients.
Another key requirement was to display billing amounts by countries and cities.
A dedicated section was also developed to provide detailed analytics for all doctors. This includes insights into the predominant types of patients each doctor treats, identifying which doctors contribute most significantly to overall revenue, and the procedures to which they most frequently refer their patients.
A specific focus was placed on visualizing the number of hospitalized patients per month and the average length of stay. Furthermore, the dashboard provides a clear view of the total billed services and outstanding receivables.

