2.	BILLING AMOUNT
 
A combined bar and line chart displays the total number of patients and the total billing amount over time. A vertical bar chart highlights that the highest billing amount was generated from X-Ray procedures, while blood tests contributed the least. The Cardiology department recorded the highest billing amount—almost twice as much as the Pediatrics department.

3.	BILLING AMOUNT – STATE AND CITY
 
Wales recorded the highest billing amount, followed by Northern Ireland in second place. When January 2025—the month with the highest billing amount—is selected, it becomes evident that the majority of patients during this period were from these two regions.

4.	DOCTORS
 
Dr. Sade Kikola treated the highest number of patients across both 2024 and 2025, accounting for 37.6% of all cases. When isolating data for 2024, Dr. Kikola's lead over other doctors becomes even more pronounced. However, in 2025, Dr. Olu Abisola have had the highest number of patients. Notably, Dr. Abisola had the highest patient satisfaction rate in 2024, and despite the increased patient load in 2025, his satisfaction rate remained consistently high.

5.	PATIENTS
 
Patient admissions, when analyzed alongside the number of days spent in the hospital—especially when filtered by specific diagnoses—provide valuable insights into the clinic’s capacity and resource utilization. The dashboard also allows for easy access to detailed information on each patient's admissions, total days hospitalized per month, payments, number of visits, and their average satisfaction rate.

6.	SATISFACTION RATE CORR WITH FACTORS
 
The scatter chart reveals a negative correlation between pending payments and patient satisfaction rate, as well as between the number of patients and satisfaction rate. However, Dr. Olu Abisola stands out as an outlier.
